{"type":"message","id":"0c8e9fbd","parentId":"06a028d3","timestamp":"2026-05-03T07:48:00.460Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_lyXrXrCWyBwKlal4JKd36568","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/opt/homebrew/lib/node_modules/openclaw/dist/extensions/acpx/node_modules/.bin/acpx\n✅ ACPX installed\n---\n0.6.1\n---\nUsage: acpx [options] [command] [prompt...]\n\nHeadless CLI client for the Agent Client Protocol\n\nArguments:\n  prompt                                  Prompt text\n\nOptions:\n  -V, --version                           output the version number\n  --agent <command>                       Raw ACP agent command (escape hatch)\n  --cwd <dir>                             Working directory (default: \"/Users/alessio/.openclaw/workspace\")\n  --auth-policy <policy>                  Authentication policy: skip or fail when auth is required\n  --approve-all                           Auto-approve all permission requests\n  --approve-reads                         Auto-approve read/search requests and prompt for writes\n  --deny-all                              Deny all permission requests\n  --non-interactive-permissions <policy>  When prompting is unavailable: deny or fail\n  --format <fmt>                          Output format: text, json, quiet\n  --suppress-reads                        Suppress raw read-file contents in output\n  --model <id>                            Agent model id\n  --allowed-tools <list>                  Allowed tool names as a comma-separated list (use \"\" for no tools)\n  --max-turns <count>                     Maximum turns for the session\n  --system-prompt <text>                  Replace the agent system prompt (claude-agent-acp via ACP _meta.systemPrompt)\n  --append-system-prompt <text>           Append text to the agent system prompt (claude-agent-acp via ACP _meta.systemPrompt.append)\n  --prompt-retries <count>                Retry failed prompt turns on transient errors (default: 0)\n  --json-strict                           Strict JSON mode: requires --format json and suppresses non-JSON stderr output\n  --no-terminal                           Do not advertise ACP terminal capability\n  --timeout <seconds>                     Maximum time to wait for agent response\n  --ttl <seconds>                         Queue owner idle TTL before shutdown (0 = keep alive forever) (default: 300)\n  --verbose                               Enable verbose debug logs\n  -h, --help                              display help for command"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":1285,"aggregated":"/opt/homebrew/lib/node_modules/openclaw/dist/extensions/acpx/node_modules/.bin/acpx\n✅ ACPX installed\n---\n0.6.1\n---\nUsage: acpx [options] [command] [prompt...]\n\nHeadless CLI client for the Agent Client Protocol\n\nArguments:\n  prompt                                  Prompt text\n\nOptions:\n  -V, --version                           output the version number\n  --agent <command>                       Raw ACP agent command (escape hatch)\n  --cwd <dir>                             Working directory (default: \"/Users/alessio/.openclaw/workspace\")\n  --auth-policy <policy>                  Authentication policy: skip or fail when auth is required\n  --approve-all                           Auto-approve all permission requests\n  --approve-reads                         Auto-approve read/search requests and prompt for writes\n  --deny-all                              Deny all permission requests\n  --non-interactive-permissions <policy>  When prompting is unavailable: deny or fail\n  --format <fmt>                          Output format: text, json, quiet\n  --suppress-reads                        Suppress raw read-file contents in output\n  --model <id>                            Agent model id\n  --allowed-tools <list>                  Allowed tool names as a comma-separated list (use \"\" for no tools)\n  --max-turns <count>                     Maximum turns for the session\n  --system-prompt <text>                  Replace the agent system prompt (claude-agent-acp via ACP _meta.systemPrompt)\n  --append-system-prompt <text>           Append text to the agent system prompt (claude-agent-acp via ACP _meta.systemPrompt.append)\n  --prompt-retries <count>                Retry failed prompt turns on transient errors (default: 0)\n  --json-strict                           Strict JSON mode: requires --format json and suppresses non-JSON stderr output\n  --no-terminal                           Do not advertise ACP terminal capability\n  --timeout <seconds>                     Maximum time to wait for agent response\n  --ttl <seconds>                         Queue owner idle TTL before shutdown (0 = keep alive forever) (default: 300)\n  --verbose                               Enable verbose debug logs\n  -h, --help                              display help for command","cwd":"/Users/alessio/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1777794480460}}
{"type":"message","id":"1771aa7b","parentId":"0c8e9fbd","timestamp":"2026-05-03T07:48:06.633Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"ACPX is installed now. But I need to go through the ACP router in OpenClaw. The skill says to use `sessions_spawn` with `runtime: \"acp\"`. Let me try spawning without the thread parameter to see if it works.\n\nBut wait — ACPX is now installed. According to the skill, after installing ACPX I should restart the gateway. Let me ask the user first since this could interrupt their session.\n\nActually, the skill says \"restart the gateway after install and offer to run the restart automatically\" but that's for the direct acpx path. Let me try the OpenClaw ACP runtime path first without installing.\n\nLet me try sessions_spawn with runtime: \"acp\" and agentId: \"codex\" to see if the OpenClaw ACP runtime can use the codex agent or if we need to configure it.\n\nActually, I think the error \"Thread bindings are unavailable for webchat\" was about the `thread: true` parameter - thread sessions aren't available in webchat. Let me try with just `mode: \"run\"` and no thread.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_NIVWbObeEVGjEweik37D5101","name":"sessions_spawn","arguments":{"runtime":"acp","agentId":"codex","mode":"run","task":"Say \"hello from codex acp\" and nothing else."}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":536,"output":343,"cacheRead":64256,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":65135,"cost":{"input":0.00007504,"output":0.00009604000000000001,"cacheRead":0.0017991679999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.001970248}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1777794480462,"responseId":"1d092e76-9b7c-47e5-8e28-1c5715e8de32"}}
