{"type":"message","id":"ec966102","parentId":"ff0b76f0","timestamp":"2026-05-03T07:48:41.270Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see! The ACP runtime has built-in agents: codex, claude, cursor, openclaw. The error \"Authentication required\" for codex probably means codex-acp isn't authenticated (it's a Zed product that needs auth). \n\nLet me try with a different agent that might not need auth. But actually, the services are embedded. Let me look at what the runtime does - it seems like it needs to figure out which agent commands to use and they need auth.\n\nActually, since installing acpx changed the plugin directory (npm install updated node_modules), I should restart the gateway for the changes to take effect. Let me check if I need to, and also explore other paths.\n\nActually, the ACP router skill says:\n- For thread-spawn ACP requests, first install acpx if missing ✅ (done)\n- Then restart the gateway and offer to run the restart automatically\n- Then retry once\n\nBut this was a thread spawn that failed. Let me try a non-thread sessions_spawn now that acpx is installed. Alternatively, let me just write the code myself - I have all the context. That might be simpler and faster.\n\nActually, looking at this more pragmatically - the ACPX runtime needs restart after install, and even then the \"Authentication required\" error might mean codex isn't set up with credentials on this machine. \n\nThe most practical approach: I'll build the backend foundation myself. I have the full Phase 2 plan, I know the tech stack, and I can write all the files directly. Let me start implementing.\n\nLet me kill the previous spawn attempt and just write the code myself.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Ho installato il runtime ACPX (era necessario), ma l'agente Codex richiede autenticazione su questa macchina. Niente paura — **scrivo io direttamente tutto il codice**. Ho il piano Phase 2 completo, conosco te