{"type":"message","id":"afb557b1","parentId":"ffb965b4","timestamp":"2026-05-03T07:55:02.323Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK! Auth works perfectly - register, login, and me all return 201/200 with proper data. \n\nThe project creation failed because I used a hardcoded \"test\" peopleId instead of a real one. The foreign key constraint violated. That's expected behavior - if I pass the actual peopleId it would work. Let me fix the test but more importantly, let me verify the create project works with a real peopleId.\n\nLet me run a proper test with the correct peopleId.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_rpWBDpPwohCLNJckY6QF2580","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /Users/alessio/.openclaw/workspace/ensoria-api && npx tsx src/index.ts 2>&1 &\nsleep 3\n\n# Login and get people ID\nTOKEN=$(curl -s -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"email\":\"admin@ensoria.app\",\"password\":\"test123\"}' | python3 -c \"import sys,json; print(json.load(sys.stdin)['data']['token'])\")\n\nPEOPLE_ID=$(curl -s http://localhost:3000/api/people -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" | python3 -c \"import sys,json; print(json.load(sys.stdin)['data'][0]['id'])\")\n\necho \"PeopleID: $PEOPLE_ID\"\necho \"\"\n\necho \"=== TEST: Create Project ===\"\ncurl -s -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/projects \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" \\\n  -d \"{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Ensoria OS MVP\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Primo progetto CRM\\\",\\\"peopleId\\\":\\\"$PEOPLE_ID\\\",\\\"value\\\":50000,\\\"stage\\\":\\\"Contact\\\"}\" | python3 -m json.tool\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== TEST: List Projects ===\"\ncurl -s http://localhost:3000/api/projects -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" | python3 -c \"import sys,json; ps=json.load(sys.stdin)['data']; print(f'Projects: {len(ps)}')\"\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== TEST: Dashboard ===\"\ncurl -s http://localhost:3000/api/dashboard -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" | python3 -m json.tool\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== TEST: Nested route (conversations) ===\"\nPROJECT_ID=$(curl -s http://localhost:3000/api/projects -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" | python3 -c \"import sys,json; print(json.load(sys.stdin)['data'][0]['id'])\")\ncurl -s -X POST \"http://localhost:3000/api/projects/$PROJECT_ID/conversations\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" \\\n  -d '{\"channel\":\"email\",\"direction\":\"inbound\",\"subject\":\"Primo contatto\",\"content\":\"Ciao! Vorrei sapere di piu sul progetto.\"}' | python3 -m json.tool\n\nkill %1 2>/dev/null\necho \"\"\necho \"=== ALL TESTS PASSED ===\"","timeout":20}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":2450,"output":740,"cacheRead":100736,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":103926,"cost":{"input":0.00034300000000000004,"output":0.00020720000000000002,"cacheRead":0.002820608,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0033708080000000003}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1777794890773,"responseId":"dfa642b4-1115-4003-927b-669be8d18e67"}}
