{"type":"message","id":"b1b05527","parentId":"a23d71c5","timestamp":"2026-05-03T08:18:21.682Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, I switched to deepseek/deepseek-v4-code. Now let me try spawning a subagent with this model. Let me give it a simpler, more focused task - just create the MCP server component and agent capabilities as additional modules on top of the existing backend.\n\nActually, let me try a much simpler approach first - spawn a subagent with deepseek-v4-code and give it a very short, focused task.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_JtCZtewTHH6YKn8ArmKM1719","name":"sessions_spawn","arguments":{"model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-code","runtime":"subagent","label":"ensoria-mcp-server","task":"Create an MCP server for Ensoria OS CRM at /Users/alessio/.openclaw/workspace/ensoria-api/src/mcp/\n\nThe MCP server should expose these tools that any AI agent can call:\n\n## Tool 1: list_people\n- Input: filters (type?, stage?, search?)\n- Calls GET /api/people internally via prisma\n\n## Tool 2: get_person  \n- Input: id\n- Calls prisma to get person by id with projects\n\n## Tool 3: create_person\n- Input: name, type?, email?, phone?, company?, stage?\n- Creates via prisma\n\n## Tool 4: list_projects\n- Input: filters (stage?, peopleId?, search?)\n- Lists projects via prisma\n\n## Tool 5: get_project\n- Input: id\n- Returns project with all nested relations\n\n## Tool 6: create_project\n- Input: name, description?, value?, stage?, peopleId\n- Creates project via prisma\n\n## Tool 7: get_dashboard_metrics\n- No input\n- Returns metrics (totalPeople, totalProjects, pipelineValue, winRate)\n\n## Tool 8: create_conversation\n- Input: projectId, channel, direction, content, subject?\n- Creates conversation entry\n\n## Tool 9: list_recent_activity\n- Input: limit? (default 10)\n- Returns recent activity log\n\n## Tool 10: get_project_health\n- Input: projectId\n- Returns aggregated health score based on conversations sentiment, milestones completion, requirements status\n\nCreate these files:\n\n1. /Users/alessio/.openclaw/workspace/ensoria-api/src/mcp/server.ts - Express-based MCP server on port 3100 that:\n   - Exposes a POST /mcp endpoint that accepts JSON-RPC style requests\n   - Request format: { method: string, params: object, id: string }\n   - Response format: { jsonrpc: \"2.0\", result: any, id: string }\n   - Each method maps to a tool handler\n\n2. /Users/alessio/.openclaw/workspace/ensoria-api/src/mcp/tools.ts - All 10 tool handler functions, each imported and using the prisma client\n\n3. /Users/alessio/.openclaw/workspace/ensoria-api/src/mcp/index.ts - Export all tools and types\n\n4. /Users/alessio/.openclaw/workspace/ensoria-api/src/mcp/types.ts - TypeScript types for MCP protocol\n\nThe server should use express (install it) and cors. Import prisma from ../../lib/prisma.js.\n\nAfter creating, the MCP server should be startable by adding `import './mcp/server.js'` to the app or by running it separately.\n\nInstall: cd /Users/alessio/.openclaw/workspace/ensoria-api && npm install express cors @types/express @types/cors\n\nDo NOT add UI files. Only create the MCP server files."}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":279,"output":836,"cacheRead":131328,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":132443,"cost":{"input":0.00003906,"output":0.00023408,"cacheRead":0.003677184,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.003950324}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1777796288137,"responseId":"4abf9a2d-82a3-44c9-99dc-0d29cd74d81f"}}
